docs/architecture/formats.md:75:- `Encoder.from_word_vectors(wv, *, tokenizer="fse_words@1", normalize=True, max_ngrams=None, oov_weight=None)` makes one of `fse.WordVectors`; FastText vectors take `max_ngrams` (default 40) and `oov_weight` (default 1), other vectors neither. `Encoder.from_arrays(vectors, *, words=..., ...)` is the same of `WordVectors.from_arrays` of its arrays. `Encoder.load(path, mmap=False)` reads one, `save` writes one (loaded data compared with the checksums they were loaded with); `encoder.word_vectors` is the table, with the fingerprint of the same tensors and keys as word_vectors 1. `Encoder.quantize(dtype)` (`"float16"` or `"int8"`) makes the encoder with the quantized copy of a float32 table, in memory (*Quantized models*).

